From 8692198066593cbe439d57a2a744da903f273000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 03:57:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ARM: dts: qcom: lg-madai: Inherit the MSM8226 USB PHY
 sequence

The recovered override copied the downstream value/absolute-address
ordering. The current binding expects offset/value pairs relative to
ULPI_EXT_VENDOR_SPECIFIC instead.

The stock Fx0 settings translate exactly to the existing SoC sequence,
so inherit it. Its first zero offset also needs the PHY driver
sequence-count fix to execute all four writes.
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai.dts | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai.dts
index 763d9dec8..1cbd183a8 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai.dts
@@ -30,6 +30,3 @@ &usb {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
-&usb_hs_phy {
-	qcom,init-seq = /bits/ 8 <0x44 0x80 0x68 0x81 0x24 0x82 0x13 0x83>;
-};
-- 
